{"audio": "james-01.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 180000, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2000, "text": "James, Chapter One."}, {"start_ms": 2000, "end_ms": 8800, "text": "James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, to the twelve tribes which are scattered abroad, greeting."}, {"start_ms": 8800, "end_ms": 16933, "text": "My brethren, count it all joy when ye fall into divers temptations; Knowing this, that the trying of your faith worketh patience."}, {"start_ms": 16933, "end_ms": 22933, "text": "But let patience have her perfect work, that ye may be perfect and entire, wanting nothing."}, {"start_ms": 22933, "end_ms": 31333, "text": "If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him."}, {"start_ms": 31333, "end_ms": 34400, "text": "But let him ask in faith, nothing wavering."}, {"start_ms": 34400, "end_ms": 39200, "text": "For he that wavereth is like a wave of the sea driven with the wind and tossed."}, {"start_ms": 39200, "end_ms": 42533, "text": "For let not that man think that he shall receive any thing of the Lord."}, {"start_ms": 42533, "end_ms": 46133, "text": "A double minded man is unstable in all his ways."}, {"start_ms": 46133, "end_ms": 56000, "text": "Let the brother of low degree rejoice in that he is exalted: But the rich, in that he is made low: because as the flower of the grass he shall pass away."}, {"start_ms": 56000, "end_ms": 68533, "text": "For the sun is no sooner risen with a burning heat, but it withereth the grass, and the flower thereof falleth, and the grace of the fashion of it perisheth: so also shall the rich man fade away in his ways."}, {"start_ms": 68533, "end_ms": 77200, "text": "Blessed is the man that endureth temptation: for when he is tried, he shall receive the crown of life, which the Lord hath promised to them that love him."}, {"start_ms": 77200, "end_ms": 90000, "text": "Let no man say when he is tempted, I am tempted of God: for God cannot be tempted with evil, neither tempteth he any man: But every man is tempted, when he is drawn away of his own lust, and enticed."}, {"start_ms": 90000, "end_ms": 96533, "text": "Then when lust hath conceived, it bringeth forth sin: and sin, when it is finished, bringeth forth death."}, {"start_ms": 96533, "end_ms": 98933, "text": "Do not err, my beloved brethren."}, {"start_ms": 98933, "end_ms": 107733, "text": "Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, and cometh down from the Father of lights, with whom is no variableness, neither shadow of turning."}, {"start_ms": 107733, "end_ms": 114800, "text": "Of his own will begat he us with the word of truth, that we should be a kind of firstfruits of his creatures."}, {"start_ms": 114800, "end_ms": 124400, "text": "Wherefore, my beloved brethren, let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, slow to wrath: For the wrath of man worketh not the righteousness of God."}, {"start_ms": 124400, "end_ms": 132667, "text": "Wherefore lay apart all filthiness and superfluity of naughtiness, and receive with meekness the engrafted word, which is able to save your souls."}, {"start_ms": 132667, "end_ms": 137867, "text": "But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves."}, {"start_ms": 137867, "end_ms": 150000, "text": "For if any be a hearer of the word, and not a doer, he is like unto a man beholding his natural face in a glass: For he beholdeth himself, and goeth his way, and straightway forgetteth what manner of man he was."}, {"start_ms": 150000, "end_ms": 161733, "text": "But whoso looketh into the perfect law of liberty, and continueth therein, he being not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work, this man shall be blessed in his deed."}, {"start_ms": 161733, "end_ms": 169867, "text": "If any man among you seem to be religious, and bridleth not his tongue, but deceiveth his own heart, this man's religion is vain."}, {"start_ms": 169867, "end_ms": 180000, "text"